FILE: init.rs
MOD: commands/init
OWNS: project scaffolding — generates .arch source files from project structure detection
PROFILE: [io]
CHANGE-FREQUENCY: volatile

run: bool → Result<(), String> [io, boundary]
  calls: scanner::detect_project_type, scan_containers, generate_system_arch, generate_deep_container_arch, generate_container_arch

scan_containers: &Path * &ProjectType → Vec<(String,String)> [io]
  note: checks candidates ["src","lib","app","packages","crates","services"]; falls back to "main"/root

generate_deep_container_arch: &Path * &str * &str → String [io]
  calls: infer_dotnet_module, infer_python_module, infer_rust_module
  note: emits .arch format (MOD:/FILE:/OWN:/BND:/DEP: blocks); deduplicates module IDs using parent-prefixed compound naming

generate_system_arch: &str * &[(String,String)] → String [pure]
  note: emits ARCH:/SYS:/DESC:/GUIDE:/CONT: block with one CONT: line per detected container

generate_container_arch: &str * &str → String [pure]

DEPENDS-ON: scanner, schema

KEY-INVARIANTS:
- init aborts if architecture/arch/system.arch already exists — no partial overwrite; users must delete to reinitialize
- writes architecture/arch/system.arch and architecture/arch/containers/{id}.arch — NOT YAML; old YAML generation is removed
- deep scan runs .NET → Python → Rust in sequence; Rust scan only runs if neither .NET nor Python found any modules
